{%- comment -%}
  Shared markup is prepended to every view before rendering, so this is where
  derived values, the vehicle diagram and reusable partials live.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  /* Charge-limit tick on the progress track. The framework has no marker
     primitive, so this is the only custom rule the plugin adds. */
  .track { position: relative; }
  .charge-limit {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 3px;
    /* currentColor so the tick inverts with the framework in dark mode */
    background: currentColor;
  }

  /* Caliper under the track spanning what the last charge session added.
     Lives outside .track because that clips its overflow. */
  .charge-session {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    height: 6px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border-left: 2px solid currentColor;
    border-right: 2px solid currentColor;
    border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor;
  }
</style>

{%- comment -%} ---------- closures ---------- {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Liquid has no array append — TRMNL's `push` filter silently returns an empty
  array — so lists are built as delimited strings and split at the end. Labels
  never contain a comma.

  Each label reads as a whole phrase, because they get joined into one sentence
  and "Front left" on its own does not say what is open.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign d = "" -%}
{%- if door_fl %}{% assign d = d | append: "Front left door," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if door_fr %}{% assign d = d | append: "Front right door," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if door_rl %}{% assign d = d | append: "Rear left door," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if door_rr %}{% assign d = d | append: "Rear right door," %}{% endif -%}
{%- assign doors_open = d | split: "," -%}

{%- assign w = "" -%}
{%- if win_fl %}{% assign w = w | append: "Front left window," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if win_fr %}{% assign w = w | append: "Front right window," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if win_rl %}{% assign w = w | append: "Rear left window," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if win_rr %}{% assign w = w | append: "Rear right window," %}{% endif -%}
{%- assign windows_open = w | split: "," -%}

{%- assign s = "" -%}
{%- if frunk %}{% assign s = s | append: "Frunk," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if tonneau %}{% assign s = s | append: "Tonneau," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if tailgate %}{% assign s = s | append: "Tailgate," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if tunnel_l %}{% assign s = s | append: "Left gear tunnel," %}{% endif -%}
{%- if tunnel_r %}{% assign s = s | append: "Right gear tunnel," %}{% endif -%}
{%- assign storage_open = s | split: "," -%}

{%- assign open = doors_open | concat: windows_open | concat: storage_open -%}
{%- assign open_count = open | size -%}

{%- if open_count == 0 -%}
  {%- assign closures_ok = true -%}
  {%- assign closure_summary = "All closed" -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign closures_ok = false -%}
  {%- assign closure_summary = open | join: " &middot; " -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if locked and closures_ok -%}
  {%- assign secure = true -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign secure = false -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- health ---------- {%- endcomment -%}

{%- if tire_fl and tire_fr and tire_rl and tire_rr -%}
  {%- assign tires_ok = true -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign tires_ok = false -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Anything the driver would want to act on. Counted so a view too small for the
  full check row can still say "2 issues".
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign issue_count = 0 -%}
{%- unless locked %}{% assign issue_count = issue_count | plus: 1 %}{% endunless -%}
{%- unless closures_ok %}{% assign issue_count = issue_count | plus: 1 %}{% endunless -%}
{%- unless tires_ok %}{% assign issue_count = issue_count | plus: 1 %}{% endunless -%}
{%- unless battery_12v_ok %}{% assign issue_count = issue_count | plus: 1 %}{% endunless -%}
{%- unless fluids_ok %}{% assign issue_count = issue_count | plus: 1 %}{% endunless -%}
{%- unless software_ok %}{% assign issue_count = issue_count | plus: 1 %}{% endunless -%}

{%- if issue_count == 0 -%}
  {%- assign health_summary = "All good" -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign health_summary = "issue" | pluralize: issue_count -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- status line ----------

  What the truck is doing, and where. Most specific state wins. `location` is a
  zone name from Home Assistant, blank when the truck is somewhere unnamed.

{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if location and location != "" -%}
  {%- assign at_place = " at " | append: location -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign at_place = "" -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if service_mode -%}
  {%- assign status_line = "In service" -%}
  {%- assign mode = "In service" -%}
{%- elsif driving -%}
  {%- assign status_line = "Driving" -%}
  {%- assign mode = "Driving" -%}
{%- elsif charging -%}
  {%- assign status_line = "Charging" | append: at_place -%}
  {%- assign mode = "Charging" -%}
{%- elsif plugged_in -%}
  {%- assign status_line = "Plugged in" | append: at_place -%}
  {%- assign mode = "Plugged in" -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign status_line = "Parked" | append: at_place -%}
  {%- assign mode = "Parked" -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- charge ---------- {%- endcomment -%}

{%- if soc <= 15 and charging == false -%}
  {%- assign low_charge = true -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign low_charge = false -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} Charge rate is only worth the pixels while current is flowing. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if charging and charge_power > 0 -%}
  {%- assign mode_detail = mode | append: " &middot; " | append: charge_power | append: " kW" -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign mode_detail = mode -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- last charge session ----------

  Plenty of people charge on a timer or a cheap-rate window, so once a session
  ends the useful question is "how much did it actually put in?". Shown only
  while the answer still describes the charge in the battery: not charging now,
  and not driven since. One drive and it is history, so it disappears.

{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign last_charge_delta = last_charge_end_soc | minus: last_charge_start_soc -%}
{%- if charging == false and moved_since_charge == false and last_charge_delta > 0 -%}
  {%- assign show_last_charge = true -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign show_last_charge = false -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign last_charge_fmt = last_charge_at | date: "%a %-I%p" -%}

{%- comment -%} Charge ETA as "1h 35m" / "45m". {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign eta_h = charge_eta_min | divided_by: 60 -%}
{%- assign eta_m = charge_eta_min | modulo: 60 -%}
{%- if eta_h > 0 -%}
  {%- assign eta = eta_h | append: "h " | append: eta_m | append: "m" -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign eta = eta_m | append: "m" -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- assign cabin_display = cabin_temp | append: "&deg;" | append: temp_unit -%}
{%- assign odometer_fmt = odometer | number_with_delimiter -%}
{%- assign updated_fmt = updated_at | date: "%-I:%M %p" -%}

{%- comment -%}
  `vehicle_label` is the plugin's custom field, so a value set in TRMNL wins over
  the name Home Assistant sends. Liquid's `default` treats "" as blank, so an
  empty field falls through.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign display_name = vehicle_label | default: vehicle | default: model -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- vehicle diagram ----------

  Top-down schematic, nose up, captured once so every view can drop it in with
  {{ vehicle_svg }}. Open closures are drawn the way they actually open rather
  than just shaded: doors swing out on their hinge, the frunk lifts past the
  nose, the tailgate drops past the tail, gear tunnels swing out the side. A
  window that is down leaves a solid gap in the door, and the tonneau's slats
  disappear when it is open. A flagged tire fills its wheel.

  The viewBox is wider and taller than the body so swung-open panels have room
  to extend outside the silhouette without clipping.

{%- endcomment -%}

{%- capture vehicle_svg -%}
<svg viewBox="0 0 180 340" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
     style="width:100%;height:100%;display:block">
  <!-- wheels; a flagged tire fills -->
  <rect x="29" y="124" width="9" height="36" rx="4" fill="{% if tire_fl %}none{% else %}currentColor{% endif %}"/>
  <rect x="142" y="124" width="9" height="36" rx="4" fill="{% if tire_fr %}none{% else %}currentColor{% endif %}"/>
  <rect x="29" y="234" width="9" height="36" rx="4" fill="{% if tire_rl %}none{% else %}currentColor{% endif %}"/>
  <rect x="142" y="234" width="9" height="36" rx="4" fill="{% if tire_rr %}none{% else %}currentColor{% endif %}"/>

  <!-- body: 104 x 288 is the R1T's real footprint ratio -->
  <rect x="38" y="26" width="104" height="288" rx="16" stroke-width="2.5"/>

  <!-- light bar across the nose -->
  <path d="M56 35 H124" stroke-width="3"/>

  <!-- frunk; lifts past the nose when open -->
  <rect x="50" y="44" width="80" height="44" rx="6"/>
  {% if frunk %}<rect x="52" y="4" width="76" height="22" rx="4" fill="currentColor"/>{% endif %}

  <!-- glasshouse; kept to two shapes so it stays readable at ~150px wide -->
  <path d="M52 94 H128 L120 112 H60 Z" stroke-width="1.5"/>
  <rect x="62" y="114" width="56" height="78" rx="4" stroke-width="1.5"/>

  <!-- doors; the leaf swings out on its hinge when open. Left doors rotate
       clockwise and right doors anti-clockwise to swing away from the body. -->
  <rect x="39" y="116" width="21" height="37" rx="3"/>
  <rect x="39" y="153" width="21" height="37" rx="3"/>
  <rect x="120" y="116" width="21" height="37" rx="3"/>
  <rect x="120" y="153" width="21" height="37" rx="3"/>
  {% if door_fl %}<rect x="33" y="116" width="5" height="37" rx="2" fill="currentColor" transform="rotate(40 38 116)"/>{% endif %}
  {% if door_rl %}<rect x="33" y="153" width="5" height="37" rx="2" fill="currentColor" transform="rotate(40 38 153)"/>{% endif %}
  {% if door_fr %}<rect x="142" y="116" width="5" height="37" rx="2" fill="currentColor" transform="rotate(-40 142 116)"/>{% endif %}
  {% if door_rr %}<rect x="142" y="153" width="5" height="37" rx="2" fill="currentColor" transform="rotate(-40 142 153)"/>{% endif %}

  <!-- windows; a lowered one leaves a gap in the door -->
  <rect x="52" y="121" width="6" height="27" rx="2" stroke-width="1.5" fill="{% if win_fl %}currentColor{% else %}none{% endif %}"/>
  <rect x="52" y="158" width="6" height="27" rx="2" stroke-width="1.5" fill="{% if win_rl %}currentColor{% else %}none{% endif %}"/>
  <rect x="122" y="121" width="6" height="27" rx="2" stroke-width="1.5" fill="{% if win_fr %}currentColor{% else %}none{% endif %}"/>
  <rect x="122" y="158" width="6" height="27" rx="2" stroke-width="1.5" fill="{% if win_rr %}currentColor{% else %}none{% endif %}"/>

  {% if body_style == "truck" %}
    <!-- gear tunnel; swings out the side -->
    <rect x="39" y="210" width="21" height="18" rx="3"/>
    <rect x="120" y="210" width="21" height="18" rx="3"/>
    {% if tunnel_l %}<rect x="19" y="211" width="19" height="16" rx="3" fill="currentColor"/>{% endif %}
    {% if tunnel_r %}<rect x="142" y="211" width="19" height="16" rx="3" fill="currentColor"/>{% endif %}

    <!-- bed; the tonneau's slats vanish when it is open -->
    <rect x="44" y="232" width="92" height="64" rx="4"/>
    {% unless tonneau %}
      <path d="M48 248 H132 M48 264 H132 M48 280 H132" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    {% endunless %}
  {% else %}
    <rect x="44" y="210" width="92" height="86" rx="4"/>
  {% endif %}

  <!-- tailgate; drops past the tail when open -->
  <rect x="44" y="298" width="92" height="12" rx="3"/>
  {% if tailgate %}<rect x="46" y="314" width="88" height="22" rx="4" fill="currentColor"/>{% endif %}
</svg>
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Front-view mark for the title bar: the vehicle's face, with the light bar that
  reads even at 28px. Not the Rivian trademark — set the plugin's Logo URL field
  to use an official asset instead.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture vehicle_mark -%}
<svg class="image" viewBox="0 0 36 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"
     style="height:100%;width:auto;display:block">
  <rect x="1.5" y="2.5" width="33" height="19" rx="6"/>
  <rect x="5" y="7" width="4.5" height="10" rx="2.25" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
  <rect x="26.5" y="7" width="4.5" height="10" rx="2.25" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
  <path d="M11.5 12 H24.5"/>
</svg>
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%} ---------- partials ---------- {%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  A labelled figure. `unit` renders smaller and tight against the value.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% template stat %}
<div class="flex flex--col flex--left gap--none">
  <span class="label label--small">{{ label }}</span>
  <div class="flex flex--row flex--bottom gap--[3px]">
    <span class="value value--small value--tnums">{{ value }}</span>
    {% if unit %}<span class="label label--small">{{ unit }}</span>{% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endtemplate %}

{%- comment -%}
  A health check. Passing checks stay quiet; failing ones invert so the eye
  lands on them first.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% template check %}
{% if ok %}
  <span class="label label--small">&#10003;&nbsp;{{ label }}</span>
{% else %}
  <span class="label label--small label--filled">&#10007;&nbsp;{{ label }}</span>
{% endif %}
{% endtemplate %}
